cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss Cognisense, please cite it as below."
title: "Cognisense: an open, offline, timing-aware cognitive task platform for low-resource settings"
abstract: >-
  Research prototype that runs five standard cognitive tasks (Go/No-Go, spatial span,
  Flanker, time reproduction, choice-delay) in a browser or on low-cost Android phones and
  classifies every metric by its robustness to device timing error. It does not diagnose
  ADHD or any other condition and has not been validated for screening.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Farzaan"
    family-names: "Jamal"
version: "0.5.0-dev"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/farzaanjamal/cognisense"
url: "https://farzaanjamal.github.io/cognisense/"
keywords:
  - cognitive assessment
  - executive function
  - reaction time
  - device latency
  - low-resource settings
  - open-source software
